				\begin{document}$${Pe}$$\end{document}Pe = 500–600025). These data suggest that vortices generated by the activity of cilia considerably enhance mass transport to and from the tissue surface in antipatharian corals. This further supports the overall benefit of epidermal ciliary beating for solute exchange in hexacorals as a group. The degree to which this mechanism improves overall metabolic performance in black corals depends on how effectively ciliary activity alleviates substrate limitation at the tissue scale.

